    stage2_aot_error_message_lost_invalid_heap_2026-09-06, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: forced a real AOT object-stage failure on a scratch build (SIMPLE_NATIVE_CPU=bogus -> llc exit 1): rc=1 and the full backend diagnostic reaches the operator at every site (raising-site prints, worker ICE receipt 1KB, native-compile-failed line, summary reason block; zero invalid-heap or lost-crossing markers; reason text 6x). Root cause (historical): old raising site interpolated err.to_text() into the returned Err; on the self-hosted binary composite Result payloads arrived misdecoded across compiled-frame returns (heap_value_to_display_string renders TAG_HEAP non-string as invalid-heap). Current tree fixes it by construction: _aot_compile_failure prints bare operands before returning (driver_aot_native_output.spl:4247), rebind-inside-the-arm at every crossing (:4540), nonempty guards (:841), plus the underlying ABI/lowering fixes; a 2-frame JIT churn probe passes under SIMPLE_JIT_STRICT_ALL=1. Deliverables: fence spec backend_aot_error_message_full_text_native_spec (SIMPLE_BINARY convention; forces the failure via SIMPLE_NATIVE_CPU in the child env; asserts wrapper + full reason + no invalid-heap) PASS on the scratch build, RED by construction on the 2026-09-06 evidence; re-verification recipe doc/07_guide/compiler/stage2_aot_error_message_reverification.md. Residuals: stage-2 lane verification needs a rebuilt stage-2 binary (the spec is the gate); a separate worker-stderr transport truncation defect (eprint_bounded drops middle bytes of large stderr, compensated by spill file + ICE receipt) deliberately left alone. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/backend/backend_aot_error_message_full_text_native_spec.spl prevention=doc/07_guide/compiler/stage2_aot_error_message_reverification.md"

